"""Write the Codex prompts for Hiro forms 2 and 3 combat sheets (attack, cast, run): form-N/<action>/prompt-used.txt.
Image 1 = form-N/source/identity-1024.png (the master on magenta), Image 2 = form-N/<action>/anchor.png (hiro_forms.py anchor)."""
from pathlib import Path

NOVICE = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
ID = {
    2: ("Hiro in his second form, the Wandering Swordsman: a chibi boy hero (he/him) with messy chestnut-brown hair and one springy cowlick tuft on top, big brown eyes; a short moss-green hooded half-cloak fastened at the neck by a round brass ring clasp, a long moss-green scarf end, a fitted brown leather jerkin with crossed straps and brass buckles over a cream shirt, ONE steel shoulder pauldron on his sword arm, steel-capped leather bracers, a belt with a square brass buckle, a small leather pouch on the belt front and a rolled parchment map case on his hip, olive-brown trousers and tall brown buckled leather boots",
        "a straight steel arming sword with a brass crossguard set with ONE small round green gem and a leather-wrapped grip", "steel sword", "cloak and scarf"),
    3: ("Hiro in his third form, the Gemwoven Hero: a chibi boy hero (he/him) with messy chestnut-brown hair and one springy cowlick tuft on top, big brown eyes; elegant light plate armour in white-gold and polished steel with gold filigree trim, a ring of four inlaid gems on the chest (red ruby, blue sapphire, green emerald, violet amethyst), small gem studs on gauntlets, knee guards and greaves, a cream tabard with gold embroidery and green side panels below a brown belt with a gold buckle, olive-brown trousers, steel-and-gold armoured boots, and a long deep moss-green cape bordered with gold woven embroidery and small diamond gems, fastened at his neck",
        "a heroic longsword with a white-steel blade whose fuller holds a woven strip of red, blue, green and violet gems, a gold crossguard shaped like spreading leaves around a large clear crystal, and a brown grip", "longsword", "cape"),
}
HEAD = """Image 1 is the exact character identity, art and SIZE reference: {id}. His weapon is EXACTLY {weapon}, the same length and width in every frame (only shortened by perspective, never a different sword). Draw the SAME boy with EXACTLY the proportions of Image 1 in every frame: the same big chibi head, the same torso, legs and boots; never draw the head bigger or smaller, never draw him taller, shorter, chibier or stockier than Image 1. His face is the face of Image 1, acting only the expression each frame asks for. No new armour pieces, no extra weapons, no extra limbs. Paint crisp clean dark outlines and a sharp face: the sheet is shown large.
Image 2 is a scale-and-root template made from the same accepted character. Preserve Image 2 exact cell locations, fixed camera distance, standing-equivalent anatomical scale, body-root position near the horizontal centre of each cell, grounded foot-contact line at about 94% of cell height, and padding. Change only the action pose in each slot. Never zoom or resize a pose to fill its cell. Head, torso, {cloth}, boots and sword size must stay identical to Image 2 in every frame. Do not reproduce Image 2 as-is and do not draw any guide, border or separator.
"""
TAIL = """Facing RIGHT in 3/4 view in every frame. Body plus {short} only: NO slash arc, NO weapon trail, NO motion lines, NO particles, NO sparks, NO glow, NO aura, NO dust (effects are a separate runtime layer). Keep the {short} and the {cloth} compact and close to the body so everything stays fully inside its own cell: nothing crosses any cell edge; leave a clear magenta margin of at least 5% on all four sides of every cell. Same camera distance and same body scale in all 6 frames.
Exactly 6 frames in a 3 columns x 2 rows grid of equal square 512x512 cells, total image 1536x1024, read left-to-right then next row. Background 100% solid flat #FF00FF magenta in every cell, no gradient, no floor, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no numbers, no gridlines, no borders, no frames between cells. Clean HD smooth painted chibi game art, NOT pixel art."""
RUN = "Create a 6-frame RUN cycle sheet: a brisk grounded forward run to the right, read as one seamless loop. He leans slightly forward, his free arm pumping, the {short} held low in his sword hand trailing a little behind his hip, blade pointing down and back; {flow}. Frame 1: contact, front boot reaching forward, back boot pushing off. Frame 2: down, weight on the front leg, knee bent. Frame 3: passing, back leg swinging through, one boot lifted. Frame 4: contact with the other leg forward. Frame 5: down on that leg. Frame 6: passing again, flowing back into Frame 1. His lowest boot touches the shared ground line in every frame; he never flies or jumps high; head and torso stay at the same height (only a small natural bob)."
ACT = {
    ("attack", 2): "Create a 6-frame ATTACK animation sheet: a quick, compact one-handed forward slash with the steel sword, body only. Frame 1: ready stance exactly like Image 1, sword held low in front, blade angled down. Frame 2: wind-up, he pulls the sword back and up across his chest to beside his far shoulder, body coiled, knees bent, determined look. Frame 3: he steps into a short forward slash, the sword swinging forward at chest height, blade pointing ahead to the right, arm extended but the blade kept within the cell. Frame 4: follow-through, the sword sweeps diagonally down in front of him, blade pointing down-forward toward the ground, torso turned slightly, cloak and scarf snapping forward. Frame 5: recoil, the sword drawn back toward his waist, blade near vertical. Frame 6: settle back to the ready stance of Frame 1. Both feet stay planted on the shared ground line throughout; the torso centre does not travel; no jump, no deep crouch.",
    ("attack", 3): "Create a 6-frame ATTACK animation sheet: a heroic, compact two-handed longsword cut, body only. Frame 1: ready stance exactly like Image 1, longsword held low in front, blade angled down. Frame 2: wind-up, he lifts the longsword in both hands up beside his far shoulder, blade nearly vertical, body coiled, knees bent, fierce look. Frame 3: the longsword raised upright in front of his face, tip only a little above his hair, leaning forward. Frame 4: a sharp diagonal downward cut in front of the body, blade pointing down-forward toward the ground beside his front boot, hilt at chest height, cape snapping forward. Frame 5: follow-through recover, sword pulled back up toward the chest, blade near vertical. Frame 6: settle back to the ready stance of Frame 1. Both feet stay planted on the shared ground line throughout; the torso centre does not travel; no jump, no deep crouch.",
    ("cast", 2): "Create a 6-frame CAST animation sheet (a rallying battle command), body only. Frame 1: ready stance exactly like Image 1, sword held low in front in his sword hand. Frame 2: he clenches his free hand into a fist in front of his chest, focused. Frame 3: he lifts the fist a little higher with a confident shout, mouth open. Frame 4: he thrusts his free hand forward, palm open toward the right, calling out. Frame 5: he holds the open-palm pose, steady, cloak lifting a little. Frame 6: he lowers the free hand back to the ready stance of Frame 1. The sword stays low in his sword hand in every frame. Feet stay planted on the shared ground line throughout.",
    ("cast", 3): "Create a 6-frame CAST animation sheet (a knightly rallying salute), body only. Frame 1: ready stance exactly like Image 1, longsword held low in front. Frame 2: he brings the longsword up in his sword hand, blade rising. Frame 3: he holds the longsword upright in front of his face in a knightly salute, the hilt at chin height, the blade pointing straight up (blade tip inside the cell), eyes closed in focus. Frame 4: eyes open, he stretches his free hand forward with the palm open toward the right, the sword still upright. Frame 5: he holds that pose, cape lifting slightly. Frame 6: he lowers the sword back to the ready stance of Frame 1. Feet stay planted on the shared ground line throughout.",
    ("run", 2): RUN.format(short="steel sword", flow="the cloak and the long scarf end stream back behind him"),
    ("run", 3): RUN.format(short="longsword", flow="the green cape streams back behind him, kept compact"),
}

if __name__ == "__main__":
    for n, (idt, weapon, short, cloth) in ID.items():
        for a in ("attack", "cast", "run"):
            text = HEAD.format(id=idt, weapon=weapon, cloth=cloth) + "\n" + ACT[a, n] + "\n\n" + TAIL.format(short=short, cloth=cloth)
            (NOVICE / f"form-{n}/{a}/prompt-used.txt").write_text(text + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    print("prompts written")
